# Code quality improvement

## Before finishing a change

```bash
pnpm run lint        # ESLint, zero warnings
pnpm run typecheck   # astro check
pnpm run format      # Prettier when touching many files
```

Pre-commit hook runs: `mcp:safety`, `pretty-quick`, `lint`, `typecheck`.

## ESLint highlights

- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: error
- `eqeqeq`: always strict equality
- `no-console`: warn (allowed: `warn`, `error`) except in `scripts/`
- Components: `no-restricted-imports` for orbitype and server env (ADR-0007)
- No hardcoded hex colours in components/pages (ADR-0008)

## Astro-specific

- Use `eslint-plugin-astro` recommended rules
- Frontmatter scripts: keep logic minimal; heavy work belongs in `src/lib/`

## Do not

- Disable ESLint rules file-wide without ADR-level justification
- Commit formatting-only churn unrelated to your task
- Skip typecheck because "it's just Astro markup" — frontmatter is TypeScript

Full gate: `pnpm run verify` (adds e2e + key leakage scan).
